Check environment configuration

Verifies that your environment is properly configured for Antithesis testing. Runs health checks — container runtime, docker compose, the tenant and repository settings, and your credentials (set in the ANTITHESIS_* environment variables). A missing tenant fails the check; a missing repository is a warning, because only a launch needs it. doctor also warns when more than one credential source is available. To see the settings that snouty resolved, run `settings_show`.

snouty prefers an API key (full API access); a username and password is deprecated auth, accepted only by `debug`.

When credentials are configured, doctor also contacts the Antithesis API to report the API and tenant versions and confirm connectivity. It warns when the tenant release is too old for an API that some commands use, and when CLI OAuth login is not enabled for the tenant. Pass `offline` to skip these network calls.

The command fails if any required check fails. With `json`, the report is one JSON object.

Examples:
  doctor
  doctor {"offline": true}
